$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Representative procedure C: Negishi cross-coupling of aryl iodides with
alkyl zinc reagents (Table 3, entry 9) and characterization data for
3s-3x: To a solution of ZnCl2 (1.60 mL, 1.60 mmol, 1.00 M in THF) was
added dropwise n-butylmagnesium chloride (0.75 mL, 1.50 mmol, 2.00 M in
THF) over 3 min at 0 °C. The solution was stirred at 0 °C for 1 h. In a
second dry N2-flushed Schlenk flask, a solution of 7a (20 mg, 2.00 mol %,
0.02 mmol) and 3- iodobenzonitrile (229 mg, 1.00 mmol) in THF (2.00 mL)
was stirred for 5 min at ambient temperature and the organozinc reagent
was added. The reaction mixture was then stirred at 60 °C for 24 h. At
ambient temperature, H2O (5.0 mL) was added. The aqueous phase was
extracted with EtOAc (2 x 10 mL). The combined organic phases were
concentrated in vacuo. Purification by column chromatography
(n-hexane/EtOAc: 100/1) yielded 3s (111 mg, 70%) as a colourless liquid.
3-n-Butyl benzonitrile (3s), yield (111 mg, 70%). 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 7.47-7.42 (m, 2H), 7.41-7.31 (m, 2H), 2.62 (t, J = 7.6 Hz,
2H), 1.65-1.51 (m, 2H), 1.41-1.18 (m, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 3H). 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 144.2 (Cq), 133.1 (CH), 131.9 (CH), 129.4 (CH),
129.0 (CH), 119.1 (Cq), 112.2 (Cq), 35.2 (CH2), 33.2 (CH2), 22.1 (CH2),
13.8 (CH3). IR (NaCl): 3059, 2956, 2359, 2229, 1590, 1468, 1105, 1073,
794 cm-1. MS (ESI) m/z (relative intensity) 182 (100) [M+Na+]. HRMS (ESI)
m/z calcd for C11H13N+Na+ 182.0940, found 182.0946. The spectral data
were in accordance with those reported in the literature.19
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kumada-Corriu cross-coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
