$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-Macrostomine (1). A solution of 11 (20 mg, 0.0652 mmol, 1.0 equiv)
and Ni(acac)2 (6.8 mg, 0.0261, 40 mol %) in dry THF (2 mL) at rt was
treated dropwise with piperonylmagnesium chloride (12) (450 μL, 0.44 M in
THF, 3.0 equiv). The mixture was stirred at rt for 4 days and then
quenched with 2 mL of saturated aqueous NaHCO3. The mixture was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (2 x 15 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over
K2CO3, filtered through Celite, and concentrated under reduced pressure
to afford the crude product. Purification by radial PLC (SiO2, 1% TEA/30%
EtOAc/hexanes) afforded 16.7 mg (63%) of amorphous 1. [α]26 D -54 (c
0.72, CHCl3); lit.5 [α]25 D -51 ± 3 (c 0.892, CHCl3); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
C6D6) δ 8.80 (s, 1H), 7.88 (s, 1H), 7.32 (s, 1H), 7.01 (d, J = 2.0 Hz,
1H), 6.78 (dd, J = 8.0, 1.2 Hz, 1H), 6.58 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (s,
2H), 4.56 (s, 2H), 3.51 (s, 3H), 3.43 (s, 3H), 3.38 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H),
3.08 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.13 (s, 3H), 2.01-2.10 (m, 2H), 1.75-1.98 (m,
2H), 1.53-1.63 (m, 1H). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.40 (s, 1H), 7.79 (s,
1H), 7.32 (s, 1H), 6.68-6.80 (m, 3H), 5.86 (s, 2H), 4.48 (s, 2H), 3.99
(s, 3H), 3.89 (s, 3H), 3.54 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 3.31 (t, J = 8.0 Hz,
1H), 2.28-2.42 (m, 2H), 2.25 (s, 3H), 1.86-2.11 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (100
MHz, CDCl3) δ 23.3, 33.4, 41.0, 42.6, 56.0, 56.1, 57.5, 68.3, 101.0,
